 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "The Body Mass Index (BMI) tells whether an adult's weight is healthy for their height.\nBMI = mass (kg) ÷ height² (m²)\nExample: mass 60 kg, height 1.6 m: BMI = 60 ÷ (1.6 × 1.6) = 60 ÷ 2.56 = 23.4.\nAdult classes (World Health Organization):\n• below 18.5: underweight\n• 18.5 to 24.9: normal (healthy) weight\n• 25 to 29.9: overweight\n• 30 and above: obese\nFor children and teenagers, the BMI is compared with charts for their age and sex, because they are still growing.\nThe BMI is only a guide: a muscular athlete can have a high BMI without too much fat.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "m": 60,
   "h": 1.6
  },
  "problem": "A woman has mass {m} kg and height {h} m. Find her BMI and say which class she is in.",
  "steps": [
   "Height² = {h} × {h} = {h * h}.",
   "BMI = {m} ÷ {h * h} = {bmi(m, h)}; this is between {18.5} and {24.9}."
  ],
  "answer": "{bmi(m, h)}: {bmiClass(bmi(m, h))}",
  "checks": []
 },
